{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Eigenpairs","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of eigenpairs, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"smallest"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"tolerance"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under Throws.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"maxIterations"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · λ, relative to itself as for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"algebraicConnectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when given, is at least 1."}]}],"name":"Precondition"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" products"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"20√n products or "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"laplacianSpectrum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}]}],"name":"Throws"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the normalized Laplacian N (","type":"text"},{"code":"normalizedLaplacianMatrix()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"= ","type":"text"},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Eigenpairs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Spectral